iate about him so much  as an actor we obviously wrote the movie  together but then once you're on set  he's a director and i'm an actor you  know and i need his support and  encouragement and i need to make him you  know he needs to make me feel like  everything's gonna be okay even in spite  of all the chaos and he really does a  remarkable job doing that yeah truly and  especially in comedy because nothing  kills a joke more than someone like  screaming like we're gonna lose the  light so he yeah he really did keep it  calm i mean no matter how tight our  schedule was if me or any of the other  actors had a bit or a joke they wanted  to try he always made sure there was  time for that  um one of the things that i found it  just it feels very natural what happens  in the movie it feels it's based on  authenticity and can you sort of talk  about maybe some of the examples of  your real life permeating into this  movie  my real life permeates into the movie in  many ways um  experiences i've had with guys  experiences close friends of mine have  had  um in romantic relationships or with sex  love dating all of it  um  experiences i've had in my professional  life  um  there's so much of me in there even  though it's not identical to me  um but  you know i i really liked the idea one  of the first ideas we started with is  the idea that a very confident  self-reliant man  or person you know um  could be undone by falling in love like  someone who really prides himself on not  needing someone both characters do that  actually and i thought what happens when  two people like that fall for each other  like how do they navigate that and i  thought there was potential for a lot of  comedy in that and also a lot of  like you know poignant moments and  romantic moments and and that was the  idea i started with that i did borrow  from my real life that i i thought could  be compelling  one of the things i love learning about  um when you're making any movie or show  is like 